prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:209:## 7. Base Skill Routing Rules
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:211:Use no skill by default if the task is tiny and the direct path is already safe and obvious.
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:213:Load one primary skill when the task materially matches its domain.
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:214:Load at most one secondary skill only when the gain is real and the overlap is clean.
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:216:Primary skills available in this project:
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:221:- `orchestration-control`
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:225:- Document-grounded investigation / latest facts / source-backed answer / evidence synthesis -> `grounded-research`
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:228:- Multi-agent / A2A / delegation topology / lifecycle coordination / agent-card or capability-orchestration work -> `orchestration-control`
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:230:Skill loading rules:
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:231:- do not load a skill merely because it exists
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:232:- do not load multiple heavy skills when one clearly fits
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:234:- prefer no skill over a weakly matched skill
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:235:- if the task changes materially, reroute
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:236:- if the main problem is coordination topology or lifecycle control, prefer `orchestration-control` over improvised delegation
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:240:External interaction exists to improve execution, grounding, or verification.
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:268:- treat `chat_only`, `retrieval_read_only`, `tool_read_write`, `cli_or_local_filesystem`, `browser_or_gui`, and `high_impact_external_action` as progressively stronger approval and verification surfaces
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:270:## 9. Retrieval, Grounding, and Evidence Discipline
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:272:Retrieval is optional but mandatory when grounding need is real.
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:274:Activate stronger grounding discipline when:
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:277:- the user asks for citations, evidence, sources, verification, or latest status
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:279:- source conflict could change the answer
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:282:- define the evidence target first
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:283:- use the smallest evidence slice that satisfies the claim
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:287:- reduce claim strength when evidence is insufficient
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:288:- do not present memory or habit as evidence authority
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:289:- do not let retrieved volume become evidence theater
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:290:- if research is multi-round or citation-heavy, keep the consulted-source surface inspectable enough that another reviewer can tell which source groups materially shaped the answer
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:293:- retrieval governs current evidence authority
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:296:- search skill governs exploration depth
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:297:- multi-agent behavior, if any, remains bounded and justified
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:312:- fresher grounded evidence outranks weaker remembered state
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:314:- retrieve only the smallest relevant remembered state
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:320:## 11. Search, Reasoning, and Planning Discipline
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:323:- direct solve first
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:326:Primary planning question:
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:334:- planning quality matters
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:340:Use explicit route choice when:
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:341:- multiple execution paths differ materially in safety, cost, evidence fit, or reversibility
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:342:- the choice between direct solve, retrieval, tool use, delegation, or propose-only can change quality
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:352:- route by task fit, not by available sophistication
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:354:- re-prioritize when evidence, budget, or scope changes materially
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:358:- do not let planning become a ceremony
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:359:- use micro-plans where possible
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:363:- replan when assumptions fail
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:365:Plan approval checkpoint:
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:366:- show the plan before execution when a multi-step path is destructive, costly, preference-sensitive, or hard to reverse
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:367:- if the plan materially changes after approval, re-check the approval boundary
prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md:370:- if the same low-gain action or edit pattern repeats without stronger validated progress, checkpoint, narrow, replan, escalate, or stop
